  "notes": "A compound verb from {分|わ}ける (to divide) + {合|あ}う (to do mutually). The {合|あ}う component adds the nuance of reciprocity — everyone participates in the sharing.\n\nCan be used for both physical items and abstract things like feelings, experiences, or burdens.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {食|た}べ{物|もの}を{分|わ}け{合|あ}う (share food)\n- {利益|りえき}を{分|わ}け{合|あ}う (share profits)\n- {苦楽|くらく}を{分|わ}け{合|あ}う (share hardships and joys)",
